From e3669b6027ac9231edb3a32bd9d57bfc1eb63630 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amphion <amphion@local>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 01:38:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(itn): keep spoken digit runs intact instead of grouping
 them
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The zh ITN tagger reads 一二三四五六七八九十 as cardinal { value: "123 4567
80~90" }: it splits the run and renders a trailing 十 as an approximate range,
so counting digits out loud came back regrouped. Collapse such a run to its
digits before tagging, and translate alignment offsets back through the
rewrite so the spans the caller receives stay in its own coordinates.
---
 .../csrc/wetext/processor/wetext_processor.cc | 131 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 125 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sherpa-onnx/csrc/wetext/processor/wetext_processor.cc b/sherpa-onnx/csrc/wetext/processor/wetext_processor.cc
index 2bf54a1f..d34940ae 100644
--- a/sherpa-onnx/csrc/wetext/processor/wetext_processor.cc
+++ b/sherpa-onnx/csrc/wetext/processor/wetext_processor.cc
@@ -12,6 +12,8 @@
